S6 — Unifying sufficiency predicate: Comparing (A) No-Rescue vs. (B) and (C) Rescue, the distinguishing condition is the functional status of MYB72. In (A), MYB72 is non-functional (null); in (B) and (C), MYB72 is functional. Therefore:
  SUFFICIENT(PHR1^{GOF} → ΔMicrobiota | background) ⟺ MYB72 is functional in that background.

S7 — Logical conclusion: In a strictly linear chain, gain-of-function at PHR1 can only restore the arrow PHR1 →^{transcriptional_activation} MYB72. It cannot circumvent a downstream lesion at MYB72 because MYB72 is the obligate downstream transducer; no bypass path exists within {PHR1, MYB72, F6'H1, Coumarins, ΔMicrobiota}. PHR1^{GOF} rescues ΔMicrobiota if and only if MYB72 is present and functional.

